# Worktree layout (mandatory)

The only top-level Jet checkout is the main clone (e.g. `…/Github/jet`).

**Forbidden**

- Creating or leaving sibling directories next to the clone: `jet-bd-*`, `jet-*`, agent-id
  directories, parallel clones, or symlinks that recreate that mess
- `git worktree add` with a path outside the main clone
- Treating a worktree’s `plugins/tower/.tower/` as the real board

**Required**

- Worktree paths only under:
  - `<repo>/.claude/worktrees/<short-name>` (preferred)
  - `<repo>/.agent-worktrees/<short-name>` (allowed)
- Create: `git worktree add .claude/worktrees/<short-name> -b <branch>`
- If a tool already created an outside path: immediately
  `git worktree move <bad-path> .claude/worktrees/<short-name>` and continue only there
- Finish: integrate, `git worktree remove`, delete temp branch
- Tower: read/write only the main checkout board via `node plugins/tower/tower.mjs`

Authority: `AGENTS.md` § Ownership and worktrees. Layout check:
`scripts/agent/check-worktree-layout.sh`.
